//! [depth-limit-getter]
Returns the maximum nesting depth of messages that deserialize() accepts.

If the input data contains messages nested deeper than this limit,
deserialize() returns \c false and lastError() returns
QAbstractProtobufSerializer::Error::InvalidFormat. This limit does not
affect serialize(). The default is the same as in the upstream C++
and Java protobuf implementations. The top-level message is not counted:
with a limit of N, a message may contain N levels of nested messages.

The value is chosen in this order:
\list 1
\li The limit set with setDeserializationDepthLimit().
\li The \c{QT_PROTOBUF_NESTING_LIMIT} environment variable, if it is
    set to a positive integer. It is read once per process, the first time
    the limit is needed. Later changes to it are not used. Any other
    value is ignored with a warning.
\li The default: \c{100}.
\endlist
//! [depth-limit-getter]

//! [depth-limit-setter]
Sets the maximum nesting depth of messages that deserialize() accepts to
\a limit. It does not affect serialize(). The \a limit must be a positive
integer; otherwise a warning is printed and the limit is not changed. This
limit is used instead of the \c{QT_PROTOBUF_NESTING_LIMIT} environment
variable.

It is recommended to bound the nesting of messages received from
untrusted sources.
//! [depth-limit-setter]
